{"name":"Navy Black","hex":"#263032","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"navy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A country's entire maritime military force, including ships and personnel.","A governmental department in charge of a country's maritime military force."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the dark blue colour of navy blue.","Belonging to the navy; typical of the navy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navy"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"Navy","blocks":[{"text":"A navy, naval force, military maritime fleet, war navy, or maritime force is the branch of a state's armed forces principally designated for naval and amphibious warfare; namely, lake-borne, riverine, littoral, or ocean-borne combat operations and related functions. It includes anything conducted by surface ships, amphibious ships, submarines, and seaborne aviation, as well as ancillary support, communications, training, and other fields."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/The_Hermione_being_escorted_by_the_USS_Mitscher_%28DDG-57%29_%281%29.jpg/330px-The_Hermione_being_escorted_by_the_USS_Mitscher_%28DDG-57%29_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navy","wikidata":"Q4508"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"},{"title":"Navy blue","blocks":[{"text":"Navy blue, also known simply as navy, is a dark shade of the color blue. The name navy blue originally referred to the color of uniforms worn by officers in the Royal Navy. In the late 18th century, the Royal Navy adopted the color for its sailors' uniforms, partly due to the practical reason that dark colors were less prone to showing dirt and wear during long sea voyages. The color became so associated with naval service that it came to be known simply as \"navy blue.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Flickr_-_Official_U.S._Navy_Imagery_-_The_Blue_Angels_fly_in_formation..jpg/330px-Flickr_-_Official_U.S._Navy_Imagery_-_The_Blue_Angels_fly_in_formation..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navy_blue","wikidata":"Q5975887"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/U_995_Laboe.JPG/500px-U_995_Laboe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/U_995_Laboe.JPG/1280px-U_995_Laboe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/U_995_Laboe.JPG/500px-U_995_Laboe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The German submarine U-995, which served during World War II, pictured in 2012.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AU_995_Laboe.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/22nd_MEU_Storms_Beach_During_Bright_Star_DVIDS212393.jpg/500px-22nd_MEU_Storms_Beach_During_Bright_Star_DVIDS212393.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/22nd_MEU_Storms_Beach_During_Bright_Star_DVIDS212393.jpg/1280px-22nd_MEU_Storms_Beach_During_Bright_Star_DVIDS212393.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/22nd_MEU_Storms_Beach_During_Bright_Star_DVIDS212393.jpg/500px-22nd_MEU_Storms_Beach_During_Bright_Star_DVIDS212393.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"US 22nd Marine Expeditionary Unit conducting a beach landing exercise.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A22nd_MEU_Storms_Beach_During_Bright_Star_DVIDS212393.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/USS_John_C._Stennis_%28CVN-74%29_and_HMS_Illustrious_%28R_06%29_in_the_Persian_Gulf_on_April_9%2C_1998.jpg/500px-USS_John_C._Stennis_%28CVN-74%29_and_HMS_Illustrious_%28R_06%29_in_the_Persian_Gulf_on_April_9%2C_1998.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/USS_John_C._Stennis_%28CVN-74%29_and_HMS_Illustrious_%28R_06%29_in_the_Persian_Gulf_on_April_9%2C_1998.jpg/1280px-USS_John_C._Stennis_%28CVN-74%29_and_HMS_Illustrious_%28R_06%29_in_the_Persian_Gulf_on_April_9%2C_1998.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/USS_John_C._Stennis_%28CVN-74%29_and_HMS_Illustrious_%28R_06%29_in_the_Persian_Gulf_on_April_9%2C_1998.jpg/500px-USS_John_C._Stennis_%28CVN-74%29_and_HMS